From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:02:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 086/147] hjviewer: the PC's connection window marks proven
 logins, shows recording
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W2 (the Rust part; docs/architecture.md 5-10): the process that takes a
connection decides what the connection manager may say about who connects
and hands it over apart from the name, in IPC Login's new hjv_mark {kind,
who} (src/hjviewer_cm.rs). An accepted same-account proof is the one record
self.hjv_proven {name, who}, set in hjv_account_login before
send_logon_response_and_keep_alive, so a login without 2FA sees it at every
step (critic 2-3; TV-W3, W5 and W9 read it). try_start_cm takes the proven
device name with the mark same-account and the list's masked owner, else
hjviewer_cm::unproven: in pinned builds the peer's name without control,
bidi and zero-width characters, marked unverified-name when, NFKC-folded
to its letters and digits, it holds 같은계정, sameaccount, 확인됨,
verified, 교직원, staff or 로그인확인. The name no longer carries
"· 같은 계정(홍*동)" (cm_name is gone). The controller's
Misc.client_record_status goes on to the CM as Data::HjvPeerRecording when
it changes; the CM sets Client.hjv_recording and updates the card through
add_connection, as the privacy-mode rollback does. The E2E's fake CM
prints "mark {kind|none}({who})" and "cm recording {on}", and
--hjv-e2e-stream takes "record". main_get_common("hjv-admin-contact") is
the believed policy's contact_ko, or "" (decisions D-1).

Pinned builds fix allow-hide-cm to N, so no setting hides the window
(TV-W2); bot to "", so a PC's two-factor codes go to no Telegram bot and
the settings can hide its row by isOptionFixed('bot') (TV-C1); and
allow-deep-link-password and allow-deep-link-server-settings to N
(TV-C6 part 3; also how Dart knows a pinned build, critic 2-7).

unicode-normalization (0.1.23, already in Cargo.lock) becomes a direct
dependency.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
